  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p><a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> and <a href=\"/people/yoko-ono/\">Yoko Ono</a> were photographed in Stockbridge, Massachusetts, on 16 February 1977. <span id=\"more-137883\"></span></p><p>They were staying at New Marlborough, MA, where George Maciunas, a founder of the Fluxus art movement, was ill with liver and pancreatic cancer.</p><p>On this day they visited a photographic studio in the back of a cosmetic store at The Mews, 36 Main Street, in Stockbridge. The photographer, Sanford Kreger, had a selection of 19th century costumes and props, and Lennon, Ono, Sean Lennon, his nanny Nishi Saimaru, and Maciunas, were photographed by Kreger.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-137888\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI4MDAiIGhlaWdodD0iODQwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgODAwIDg0MCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"137888\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1200,1261\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon and Yoko Ono, 16 February 1977\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05-914x960.jpg\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05-914x960.jpg\" alt=\"John Lennon and Yoko Ono, 16 February 1977\" width=\"800\" height=\"840\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-137888\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/770216-john-lennon-yoko-ono_05-914x960.jpg 